ddit detail and impact file summari impact file tree graph http app codecov io gh open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 graph tree svg width 650 height 150 src pr token p6f3w9wa7q utm _ medium referr utm _ sourc github utm _ content comment utm _ campaign pr comment utm _ term open telemetri http app codecov io gh open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 src pr el tree utm _ medium referr utm _ sourc github utm _ content comment utm _ campaign pr comment utm _ term open telemetri diff coverag diff main 8014 coverag 78 5 78 6 file 185 185 line 14760 14754 6\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"f5063c965cee2c65\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32366266625879175, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10634552322684536, \"vector_similarity\": 0.830736, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"> \\\"Contexts form a tree... Successive calls to WithValue, WithCancel, WithDeadline, or WithTimeout derive new contexts.\\\"\\n\\nContexts are meant to flow forward, not be \\\"restored\\\" backward. The library shouldn't enforce this opinion.\\n\\n2. Most users want otelgin early in the chain\\n\\nI (and I assume most users) place otelgin as one of the first middleware specifically so child spans can be created from it:\\n\\nr.Use(otelgin.Middleware(\\\"my-service\\\"))  // ← First - creates root span\\n\\nr.Use(loggingMiddleware)                  // ← Creates child spans\\n\\nr.Use(authMiddleware)                     // ← Creates child spans\\n\\nr.GET(\\\"/\\\", handler)                       // ← Handler creates child spans\\n\\nCommon use cases that need the parent span:\\n\\n- Database transactions with tracing\\n\\n- Inter-service HTTP calls with trace propagation\\n\\n- Structured logging with trace IDs\\n\\n- Background jobs that need trace context\\n\\nYour example breaks all of these - they'd have no parent span.\\n\\n3. Users can control span isolation themselves \\n\\nIf a user doesn't want their spans to be children of otelgin's span, they can do exactly what the defer does - but explicitly:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nvar tracer = otel.Tracer(instrumentationName)\\n\\nfunc myCustomMiddleware(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n    ctx, span := tracer.Start(c.Request.Context(), \\\"myCustomMiddleware\\\")\\n\\n    defer span.End()\\n\\n    c.Next() // runs otelgin and other middleware\\n\\n    // Explicitly restore context if the user doesn't want child spans and since the user is in control of goroutines the onus is on them to do so safely (as it should be)  \\n\\n    c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\nThis gives users control without the library making opinionated (and race-prone) decisions.\\n\\nEven if we agreed on the semantics, I'm not sure of a safe way of doing it from a library implementation.\\n\\nBottom line: The defer enforces an anti-pattern, breaks the common use case (otelgin as root span), prevents valid patterns (goroutines with trace context), and causes data races.\\n\\nUsers who need span isolation can manage it themselves without the library making unsafe assumptions.\\n\\nWhat do you think? I'm happy to add documentation showing how users can achieve span isolation if they need it. \\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-14T08:42:01Z\\n\\nI disagree with this being a violation of Go's conventions (in the context of the middleware pattern, we don't flow forward. At the end of a middleware, we go back to its parent).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"context form a tree success call to withvalu withcancel withdeadlin or withtimeout deriv new context context are meant to flow forward not be restor backward the librari shouldn t enforc this opinion 2 most user want otelgin earli in the chain i and i assum most user place otelgin a one of the first middlewar specif so child span can be creat from it r use otelgin middlewar my servic first creat root span r use loggingmiddlewar creat child span r use authmiddlewar creat child span r get handler handler creat child span common use case that need the parent span databas transact with trace inter servic http call with trace propag structur log with trace id background job that need trace context your exampl break all of these they d have no parent span 3 user can control span isol themselv if a user doesn t want their span to be child of otelgin s span they can do exact what the defer doe but explicit go var tracer otel tracer instrumentationnam func mycustommiddlewar c gin context ctx span tracer start c request context mycustommiddlewar defer span end c next run otelgin and other middlewar explicit restor context if the user doesn t want child span and sinc the user is in control of goroutin the onus is on them to do so safe a it should be c request c request withcontext ctx this give user control without the librari make opinion and race prone decis even if we agre on the semant i m not sure of a safe way of do it from a librari implement bottom line the defer enforc an anti pattern break the common use case otelgin a root span prevent valid pattern goroutin with trace context and caus data race user who need span isol can manag it themselv without the librari make unsaf assumpt what do you think i m happi to add document show how user can achiev span isol if they need it dmathieu 2025 10 14t08 42 01z i disagre with this be a violat of go s convent in the context of the middlewar pattern we don t flow forward at the end of a middlewar we go back to it parent\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"117632d14a67a5d4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32365822131410005, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11951074187728582, \"vector_similarity\": 0.80000234, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"opentelemetry-go-contrib pull request #8014 otelgin context save restore closed reason\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
